          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to blame, then the Marathi for to accuse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मात्र",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मात्र — mātra — \"however; though\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घर लहान आहे, मात्र खूप स्वच्छ आहे. ghar lahān āhe, mātra khūp svaccha āhe. The house is small; it is very clean, though."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often after the first word: मी मात्र (mātra) घरीच राहिलो, I, however, stayed home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मात्र (mātra) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit mātra, \"measure\", which at the end of a compound meant \"nothing but, only\" (Monier-Williams); Marathi uses it on its own for \"only\" and \"however\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
